A||||14||Spektrum-87GT||painting interior vinyl?||||1||
Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||08-26-2001||07:06 PM||||I'm thinking about switching my gray interior to a red/black interior scheme. I was wondering if anyone has painted their interior vinyl before and how does it turn out? thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||08-26-2001||07:20 PM||||I did red/black..it looks pretty good..but prep the serfaces really good with acetone..and make sure you put nice even coats on..or it will look funny in sunlight.<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-26-2001||07:36 PM||||you will need to go to a shoe store and get dye It comes in sray can and I think its put out by kiwi||||reg||1
Z||000003||PAUL88GT||08-26-2001||08:50 PM||||I used SEM brand vinyl paint and clear coat with good results on my 86SE restoration.  You will most likely have to go to an auto-body supply shop to find it.  It cost about $9 a can.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||08-26-2001||09:17 PM||||Prep the heck out of it with acetone, for the flexible parts (center console and arm rests) make sure the paint you use is specifically for flexible surfaces. The color I painted mine was a dash color from PPG but on those areas I had to use a flexible vinyl spray base cpat from auto zone. <BR>Honestly, it's great for a show car, but I've been driving my car to work a little this summer and when it sits out in the heat, then I'm getting in and out of it constantly, it's been cracking a bit. I wouldn't necessarily suggest painting the interior of a daily driver, unless you don't mind doing touchup.<BR>I re-painted or replaced every surface of my entire interior from beige to gray and altho I like it more, it's kinda a pain to have to touch up every once in a while. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-26-2001||09:33 PM||||I used plain, black Rustoleum about a month ago.  My car is definitely a daily driver and I haven't had any problems so far.  The paint holds up well to my fat @$$ getting in and out.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bluebottlejunky||08-26-2001||10:07 PM||||hahaha monkey.... agree, my seats must hate my big butt!<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B>||||reg||1
