Z||000009||fieroburton||08-27-2001||01:11 PM||||i did mine about a mont ago and had no problom just got sick  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>so use a nose and mouth filter so you dont inhale the stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>but mine turned out real good im getting <BR>mr. mikes seats to match when im out of dept.<BR>i used stuff called plasti-cout from pep boys<BR>and it does real goog but i have to touch up about 3 times a mounth but its not a problom  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>can you dye the carpet black ?<BR>i havent don that yet so can it be don ?||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||08-27-2001||04:10 PM||||VHT makes an aerosol penetrating color dye that works very well. Some auto parts stores carry it or you can get it online from summit racing for about $4.69/can. I have also used Duplicolor brand from Autozone with good results.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Loki||08-27-2001||04:32 PM||||I used DupliColor on mine  Loos great<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/loki-mg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/loki-mg</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>http://members.home.net/loki-mg||||reg||1
Z||000012||David Bartlett||08-27-2001||04:45 PM||||I painted my interior black using U-Fix-It, Vinyl Colour from Canadian Tire. I preped the surfaces with Rubbing Alcohol.<P>Outcome: It looks amazing, the hard sufaces, turn out beatiful and never need a touch-up. I only touch up the arm rests and centre console every month. Some time you need to touch up a cornor or two.||||reg||14
Z||000013||David Bartlett||08-27-2001||04:48 PM||||Oh and Carpets. I tried the spray carpet dye by U-Fix-It. It sucks and rubs off. I also tried T-shirt Black dye from Shoppers.. it worked but was not dark enough.<P>Use: Trimclad Rust Paint (black) and paint it on with a brush. It smells bad for about 2 weeks but it will never come off.||||reg||1
